Cage: dock the on-screen keyboard along the bottom of the screen.

Cage maximises every toplevel, so the full-screen keyboard hid the application
it types into. A toplevel with app-id couchliteos-osk is placed instead as a
panel across the full width and the bottom 40% (at least 240 px) of the output
showing the application it types into (of the whole output layout when that is
not known), and is kept above every other view, even one mapped or raised
(wlrctl toplevel focus) while it is open. It takes the keyboard focus when it
maps and seat_set_focus keeps it there while it is open, whatever asks for the
focus (a click, an activation request, a view mapped or destroyed): the view
asking only moves to the front of server->views, so when the keyboard closes
view_destroy focuses it, and otherwise the view that was focused before.
Fullscreen requests from the keyboard are ignored. Cage 0.2.0 has no
wlr-layer-shell, hence the app-id.
Applied after cage-0.2.0-foreign-toplevel.patch (it uses its request_activate)
with patch -p1 by config/live-build/hooks/live/0050-cage.hook.chroot.

diff -ruN a/seat.c b/seat.c
